cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Divisible-Sandpile-Percolation: a Lean 4 formalization of Quantitative explosion and percolation of the divisible sandpile"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the paper "Quantitative
  explosion and percolation of the divisible sandpile" (Bou-Rabee and
  Panagiotis, arXiv:2609.02829): for every d >= 2 the toppled set of the
  divisible sandpile percolates for every mean close enough to one
  (Theorem 1.1), the level sets {u_t > c h(t)} of the finite-time odometer at
  mean one percolate at an explicit dimension-dependent scale h(t)
  (Theorem 1.2), and the quantitative explosion and scaling results at mean
  one in every dimension (Theorem 1.3), together with every lemma,
  proposition and corollary of the paper.  The results the paper cites
  without proof are taken as explicit hypotheses.  The development contains
  no sorry and no custom axiom.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - divisible sandpile
  - percolation
  - optimal stopping
  - membrane model
license: Apache-2.0
